Payments move value through authorisation, processing, clearing, and settlement with different participants and risks.|A payment is authorised but later fails settlement.|Authorisation equals final settlement automatically?|No|Yes|Only digitally
Issuers serve cardholders; acquirers serve merchants; interchange reallocates specified fees within network rules.|A merchant fee includes several components, not just processor profit.|The entire merchant fee is interchange?|No|Yes|Only for credit cards
UPI enables specified instant account-to-account payment interactions through participating providers and infrastructure.|A user sends funds between eligible bank accounts via a UPI application.|The app necessarily becomes the legal owner of the funds?|No|Yes|Only for QR payments
Wallets store specified value or credentials; remittances transfer funds; cross-border payments add currency and compliance steps.|A low advertised fee hides an unfavourable FX spread.|Compare…?|Total delivered amount and costs|Only the headline fee|Only app ratings
Gateways support payment communication; aggregators can coordinate merchant acceptance and settlement under applicable structures.|A merchant integrates one service to accept several payment methods.|Service branding alone defines custody and settlement risk?|No|Yes|Only online
Digital lending uses electronic origination and data; alternative underwriting requires validation, privacy, and fairness controls.|A model uses behavioural data to predict repayment.|More data automatically means better credit decisions?|No|Yes|Only with AI
Embedded finance integrates financial services into other journeys; BaaS supplies infrastructure through governed partnerships.|A commerce app offers a bank-partner account.|The front-end app always bears every regulated obligation alone?|No|Yes|Only for startups
Open banking and account aggregation share authorised financial data under applicable consent and access frameworks.|A user permits limited account-data access for a defined purpose.|Consent to data access automatically authorises fund transfers?|No|Yes|Only if digital
Robo-advice automates portfolio recommendations and implementation under stated assumptions and controls.|A questionnaire assigns an allocation that needs monitoring as circumstances change.|Automation removes suitability and model risks?|No|Yes|Only with diversified ETFs
Insurtech, regtech, and wealthtech apply technology to insurance, compliance, and investing processes.|Software flags reporting anomalies for human review.|A flag proves a breach without investigation?|No|Yes|Only at high confidence
Financial identity and fraud detection combine verification, signals, controls, and investigation.|A device change raises risk but can reflect a legitimate customer.|Maximising detection alone is enough?|No: false positives also matter|Yes|Only for payments
Distributed ledgers coordinate records across participants; governance and consensus determine trust assumptions.|A shared ledger records a token transfer.|A ledger entry guarantees the represented real-world asset exists?|No|Yes|Only if public
Cryptoasset economics depend on utility, issuance, rights, incentives, and governance; token price need not imply productive cash flows.|New tokens dilute holders without adding equivalent benefits.|Scarcity alone establishes intrinsic value?|No|Yes|Only with fixed supply
Stablecoins target reference values through varied mechanisms; CBDCs are central-bank digital liabilities under their designs.|A reserve-backed token depends on reserve quality and redemption access.|A peg promise removes run and depeg risk?|No|Yes|Only in dollars
DeFi uses programmable protocols; lending and AMMs introduce collateral, oracle, governance, and smart-contract risks.|An AMM liquidity position changes as relative asset prices move.|Liquidity-provider fees guarantee a positive net return?|No|Yes|Only in large pools
Tokenisation represents rights digitally; legal enforceability, custody, and underlying asset verification remain essential.|A token purports to represent a building interest.|Token creation automatically creates enforceable ownership?|No|Yes|Only on a blockchain
Fintech economics combine volume, take rates, retention, losses, compliance, and infrastructure costs.|₹100 transaction volume at 1% take rate gives ₹1 revenue before costs.|Transaction volume equals profit?|No|Yes|Only at scale
